              "text": "If you are looking to shop the **Spiegel Home Catalog** online, the short answer is that **Spiegel is no longer in business, and there is no active, official Spiegel online store.** \n\n### What Happened to the Spiegel Catalog?\n* **The Transition to Digital:** After facing financial difficulties and multiple ownership changes in the 2000s, Spiegel discontinued its iconic print mail-order catalogs in 2012 to focus entirely on digital e-commerce (`spiegel.com`). \n* **The Final Closure:** Despite attempts to reinvent itself as an online-only fashion and home retailer, the brand could not compete with modern e-commerce giants like Amazon and Wayfair. In **2019**, the Spiegel website was shut down and the company permanently ceased all operations. \n\n---\n\n### Where to Find Spiegel Remnants Today\nIf you are looking for Spiegel for nostalgic reasons or are a collector, you can still find parts of its history online:\n* **Vintage Catalogs:** If you want to buy physical copies of retro Spiegel Home catalogs (highly sought-after for Mid-Century Modern home decor inspiration), you can find them on resale sites like **[eBay](https://www.ebay.com)** or **[Etsy](https://www.etsy.com)**. \n* **Digital Archives:** You can browse and read full digital scans of historical Spiegel catalogs (from the 1960s through the 1990s) for free on the **[Internet Archive](https://archive.org)**.\n\n---\n\n### Similar Home & Fashion Alternatives\nSince Spiegel is defunct, shoppers looking for a similar \"shop-from-the-couch\" experience with a mix of home decor, kitchen gadgets, bedding, and cozy apparel can check out these active online catalog retailers:\n\n1. **[Montgomery Ward](https://www.wards.com):** A classic rival of Spiegel that successfully transitioned to the digital age. They still operate a robust online store and mail catalogs featuring furniture, home decor, electronics, and kitchen goods. \n2. **[BrylaneHome](https://www.brylanehome.com):** Excellent for colorful bedding, bath products, outdoor furniture, and home organization solutions. \n3. **[The Lakeside Collection](https://www.lakeside.com):** Perfect for budget-friendly home decor, seasonal accents, unique gifts, and household goods. \n4. **[Miles Kimball](https://www.mileskimball.com):** A long-standing catalog retailer known for clever kitchen gadgets, home solutions, and personalized gifts. \n5. **[Country Door](https://www.countrydoor.com):** Specializes in rustic, farmhouse, and cozy home decor, furniture, and textiles with a strong mail-order heritage.",
